# Appendix B of the Reference Manual: Configuration.
# The appendix is kept in three files that this one includes.
.doc Strata Reference: Appendix B, Configuration
.chapter B
.h1 Configuration [appcfg]
This appendix describes everything that Strata keeps for the user between
runs and everything that Strata reads at start: the settings
directory and the files in it, every key of the file {c:config} with its
allowed values and its default, the panels that read and write the keys, the
list of fonts for printing, the places where the programs look for the
Editor, templates and helper programs, and what each program reads at start,
in order.  The options and the environment variables of every program are in
{n:appcmd}; the Setup panel of the Document Manager is described field by
field in {x:str-setup}.
.ix Configuration
.ix Settings of the user
.ix Setup files
.ix .strata
The sections follow the life of a setting: the place where settings are kept
and the rules that protect it ({n:appcfg-dir}, {n:appcfg-files}); the file, its
format and its keys, which a user may edit by hand ({n:appcfg-format},
{n:appcfg-keys}); the panels that write the keys and the messages of a failed
save ({n:appcfg-write}, {n:appcfg-setup}, {n:appcfg-options}); the two other
sources of settings, the font list and the search paths ({n:appcfg-fonts},
{n:appcfg-search}); and last what is not a setting, and a table of problems
({n:appcfg-notin}, {n:appcfg-examples}).
.ix Home directory
Strata keeps little.  The settings of the user are one line to a key in one
text file, from a dozen lines up to about fifty when many colors are changed,
and the list of fonts is twenty lines in another.
Everything about a document (its formats, page layout, fonts used, markers)
is stored in the document itself and not in the directory of the user; see
{x:appcfg-notin}.
.include appcfg1.src
.include appcfg2.src
